  1	//! closure_nested.rs — the gap-insensitive factoring floor, nested in IMASM.
  2	//!
  3	//! New build; the CUDA `gpu_kernel closure` floor and the CPU `phase` floor are
  4	//! untouched. The closure-height walk is the floor that stays flat across the
  5	//! prime gap: its length is the 2-adic unit group order — 2^(m-3) positions per
  6	//! coset, four cosets {1,3,-1,-3}, so 2^(m-1) candidates total — set by the band
  7	//! width m and never by q-p. Fermat's phase walk is O(q-p); this is O(2^m) with
  8	//! the same count for adjacent and for ratio-2 primes.
  9	//!
 10	//! The whole computation sits inside one ∈…∋ dyad. Everything nested between the
 11	//! split and the fuse is hidden from the system and surfaces as a single output:
 12	//! the factor. The word below carries all twelve marks; every step (P <- 9P
 13	//! mod 2^m, Q <- Q·inv9 mod 2^m, the closure test P·Q == N) runs between ∈ and ∋.
 14	//!
 15	//! Arithmetic is WordTape word-walk throughout: the value IS its glyph word, each
 16	//! bit one closed parity branch, and no BigUint and no limb vector appears inside
 17	//! the walk. BigUint touches only the boundary where the caller hands N in and
 18	//! takes the factor out.
 19	
